# L4 0-bis, passo 5 (29 settembre 2026, docs/plans/l4-upgrade.md) — GLI ALTRI
# MONDI. «Marco thinks that P» apre il mondo di Marco e P si rilegge DENTRO quel
# mondo con i lettori che esistono: parrot0 lo attribuisce, non lo crede. Il
# mondo di un altro si interroga («What does Marco think?», «Does Marco think
# that P?»), si traccia («Whose idea is that?») e si trasferisce per nome
# («Make Marco's view yours.»). «I think that P» e' il mondo di chi parla.

!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test il pensiero di un altro sta nel suo mondo]
!timeout 4
> What does Marco think?
<~ Nobody has told me what marco thinks yet.
> Marco thinks that tea tastes sour.
<~ I see: that is Marco's view: tea tastes sour. I keep it as Marco's, not as mine.
!query holds_in(world_of(marco), fact(taste, tea, sour))
!query! taste(tea, sour)
!query context(world_of(marco), reported_belief)
> Does tea taste sour?
<! Yes
> What does Marco think?
<~ Marco thinks that tea tastes sour.
> Whose idea is that?
<~ Marco's view: tea tastes sour; I keep it as theirs, not as mine.

[test la domanda su un altro mondo: suo, mio, di nessuno]
!timeout 4
> Does Marco think that tea tastes sour?
<~ Yes, that is Marco's view: tea tastes sour.
> Does Marco think that milk tastes sour?
<~ Not that I know: nobody told me so.
> Coffee tastes bitter.
> Does Marco think that coffee tastes bitter?
<~ I don't know that it is theirs: nobody told me so. I do hold that coffee tastes bitter myself.
# il mondo di prova si svuota dopo la domanda
!query! holds_in(asked(world_of(marco)), fact(taste, coffee, bitter))
!query! holds_in(asked(world_of(marco)), fact(taste, tea, sour))
!query! holds_in(world_of(marco), fact(taste, milk, sour))

[test il trasferimento da un mondo nominato]
!timeout 4
> Make Marco's view yours.
<~ Done: from now on I hold it too, not only as Marco's: tea tastes sour.
> Does tea taste sour?
<~ Yes
> Whose idea is that?
<~ you then made it mine too
> Forget that you made it yours.
<~ Done: I no longer hold it myself; it stays yours: tea tastes sour.
!query! taste(tea, sour)
!query holds_in(world_of(marco), fact(taste, tea, sour))

[test io penso che: il mondo di chi parla]
!timeout 4
> I think that milk tastes sour.
<~ I see: that is your view: milk tastes sour. I keep it as yours, not as mine.
!query holds_in(world_of(user), fact(taste, milk, sour))
> Now make it yours.
<~ Done: from now on I hold it too, not only as yours: milk tastes sour.
!reset

[test in italiano]
!set PARROT0_LANG=it
!timeout 4
> Marco pensa che il cane è un animale.
<~ Capito: Marco la pensa così: cane è un animale. Lo tengo come idea di Marco
> Che cosa pensa Marco?
<~ Marco pensa che cane è un animale.
> Fai tua l'idea di Marco.
<~ Fatto: d'ora in poi lo tengo anch'io, non solo come idea di Marco: cane è un animale.
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
